  "id": "mental-balance",
  "term": "mental balance",
  "definition": "In this historical source, mental balance means the current state of equilibrium among the brain or nerve-centres that underlies a person’s mental condition and outward expression. A fixed mental balance refers to a state in which this equilibrium is held rigidly, with little spontaneity or readiness to respond.",
